\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Co-simulation toolchain. Top row: the three input sources (C firmware, the NEORV32 VHDL SoC plus the project's VHDL CFS wrapper, and the Verilog ASCON RTL). The C firmware is cross-compiled to a RISC-V binary; the NEORV32 VHDL is elaborated through \texttt  {ghdl synth} to a single Verilog netlist; both feed Verilator together with the project's Verilog ASCON sources, producing a cycle-accurate C++ model. Running the model emits a UART log that is parsed into a Markdown cosim report.}}{14}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cosim-flow}{{5}{14}{Co-simulation toolchain. Top row: the three input sources (C firmware, the NEORV32 VHDL SoC plus the project's VHDL CFS wrapper, and the Verilog ASCON RTL). The C firmware is cross-compiled to a RISC-V binary; the NEORV32 VHDL is elaborated through \texttt {ghdl synth} to a single Verilog netlist; both feed Verilator together with the project's Verilog ASCON sources, producing a cycle-accurate C++ model. Running the model emits a UART log that is parsed into a Markdown cosim report}{figure.5}{}}
